WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:18.758
Sherlock and I were sitting near the fireplace in our Baker Street lodgings.

2
00:00:18.778 --> 00:00:21.059
"Would you like a pinch of snuff, Watson?"

3
00:00:21.399 --> 00:00:21.940
asked Holmes.

4
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:26.682
The detective held out a gold snuffbox with a large amethyst in the center of the lid.

5
00:00:27.522 --> 00:00:31.544
The ornate box was such a contrast to Holmes' simple way of life that I had to comment

6
00:00:31.624 --> 00:00:31.804
on it.

7
00:00:32.704 --> 00:00:33.985
"Where did you get this snuffbox?"

8
00:00:34.405 --> 00:00:34.825
I asked.

9
00:00:35.705 --> 00:00:39.707
"It's a little present from the king of Bohemia in return for my assistance with the Irene Adler

10
00:00:39.727 --> 00:00:41.408
case." "And the ring?"

11
00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:45.029
I asked, glancing at the remarkable diamond that sparkled upon his finger.

12
00:00:45.049 --> 00:00:50.471
"It was from the reigning family of Holland for helping with a matter of extreme delicacy," said Holmes.

13
00:00:50.491 --> 00:00:54.953
"I can't confide the details to anyone, not even you, my dear Watson."

14
00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:57.434
"Are you working on anything special right now?"

15
00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:58.294
I asked him.

16
00:00:58.314 --> 00:01:01.896
"I have ten or twelve cases that are important," he replied.

17
00:01:02.732 --> 00:01:03.953
"But none of them are interesting."

18
00:01:04.854 --> 00:01:06.975
Holmes rose from his chair and went over to the window.

19
00:01:06.995 --> 00:01:09.937
"However I may soon have an interesting one.

20
00:01:10.838 --> 00:01:12.139
Look down there on the sidewalk."

21
00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.100
I went over to the window.

22
00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.842
A tall young woman stood across the street.

23
00:01:17.782 --> 00:01:20.564
She was wearing a black jacket trimmed with matching beads and fringe.

24
00:01:21.525 --> 00:01:26.388
Her gray, broad-brimmed straw hat was accented with a red feather, and a heavy fur boa was wrapped

25
00:01:26.428 --> 00:01:27.029
around her neck.

26
00:01:27.949 --> 00:01:31.612
"She seems to have some money, although not the best taste in clothing," I commented.

27
00:01:33.132 --> 00:01:36.333
The woman nervously peeped at our windows and played with the buttons on her gloves.

28
00:01:37.393 --> 00:01:39.974
Suddenly she plunged across the street and rang our doorbell.

29
00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.435
In a few moments our landlady, Mrs.

30
00:01:42.475 --> 00:01:44.995
Hudson, announced our visitor: Miss Mary Sutherland.

31
00:01:45.896 --> 00:01:47.796
Holmes welcomed the woman and asked her to sit down.

32
00:01:48.636 --> 00:01:49.837
Then he studied her for a minute.

33
00:01:49.857 --> 00:01:54.258
"With your poor eyesight, do you find that it's difficult to use a typewriter for so many hours

34
00:01:54.318 --> 00:01:54.598
a day?"

35
00:01:54.938 --> 00:01:55.378
he asked.

36
00:01:55.398 --> 00:02:00.520
"I did at first, but now I know where the letters are without looking," Miss Sutherland said quickly.

37
00:02:01.376 --> 00:02:06.080
Then, suddenly realizing what Holmes had said, she looked at him with both fear and astonishment in her

38
00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.282
eyes. "How did you know all that about me?"

39
00:02:09.622 --> 00:02:10.103
she asked.

40
00:02:10.123 --> 00:02:13.825
"I have trained myself to see what others overlook," said Holmes.

41
00:02:13.845 --> 00:02:18.469
"There is a small dent on either side of your nose that could only be made by eyeglasses.

42
00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:21.050
Your dress sleeves have purple velvet cuffs.

43
00:02:21.991 --> 00:02:25.414
I can see a line a little above your wrist, where a typist would press her arm against

44
00:02:25.454 --> 00:02:25.894
the table."

45
00:02:25.914 --> 00:02:28.256
"I am impressed," I said.

46
00:02:29.224 --> 00:02:32.645
"I also noticed that Miss Sutherland must have left home in a hurry this morning because she is

47
00:02:32.665 --> 00:02:35.186
wearing two boots that do not match," said Holmes.

48
00:02:35.206 --> 00:02:40.487
"Plus, one boot is fastened only at the first and second buttons, and the other at the first,

49
00:02:40.607 --> 00:02:41.728
third, and fifth buttons.

50
00:02:42.668 --> 00:02:45.509
But never mind all this; it's my business to notice these things.

51
00:02:46.529 --> 00:02:48.270
Why have you come to consult me, Miss Sutherland?"

52
00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:55.252
Looking a bit dazed by Holmes' powers of observation, Miss Sutherland blurted out her reasons for appearing at

53
00:02:55.312 --> 00:02:55.812
our lodgings.

54
00:02:56.832 --> 00:03:00.714
"A friend recommended you because you found her husband after the police had assumed he was dead," she

55
00:03:00.754 --> 00:03:02.494
replied. "Oh, Mr.

56
00:03:02.554 --> 00:03:04.495
Holmes, I wish you could do the same for me!

57
00:03:05.456 --> 00:03:08.757
I have an income of one hundred pounds per year in addition to the money I make with

58
00:03:08.797 --> 00:03:09.477
my typewriter.

59
00:03:10.358 --> 00:03:12.278
I would give it all to know what has become of Mr.

60
00:03:12.338 --> 00:03:13.099
Hosmer Angel."

61
00:03:13.119 --> 00:03:15.880
"Why were you in such a hurry to come here this morning?"

62
00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:16.760
asked Holmes.

63
00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:22.162
"Mr. Windibank—that is, my father—would not go to the police, and he would not consult you," said Miss

64
00:03:22.182 --> 00:03:25.984
Sutherland. "He wouldn't do anything and kept saying no harm had been done.

65
00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.701
That made me so angry that I just threw on my things and came straight here."

66
00:03:29.721 --> 00:03:33.843
"You and your father have different last names," said Holmes.

67
00:03:33.863 --> 00:03:36.544
"Mr. Windibank must be your stepfather."

68
00:03:36.564 --> 00:03:38.645
"Yes, he is my stepfather.

69
00:03:39.565 --> 00:03:43.027
I call him my father although that sounds strange because he is only five years older than I

70
00:03:43.127 --> 00:03:45.068
am." "And your mother is alive?"

71
00:03:45.088 --> 00:03:47.529
"Oh yes, Mother is alive and well.

72
00:03:48.409 --> 00:03:52.991
I wasn't pleased when she married again so soon after Father's death, especially when she married a man

73
00:03:53.071 --> 00:03:54.432
fifteen years younger than herself."

74
00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:58.883
Miss Sutherland explained that her father had been a plumber with a profitable business.

75
00:03:59.864 --> 00:04:02.426
With the help of the foreman, her mother continued running the business.

76
00:04:02.446 --> 00:04:04.348
"But when she married Mr.

77
00:04:04.368 --> 00:04:06.710
Windibank, he made her sell it," said Miss Sutherland.

78
00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:11.834
"He is in the wine business, working for the importers Westhouse and Marbank of Fenchurch Street.

79
00:04:13.475 --> 00:04:15.697
He felt that the plumbing business was beneath him socially."

80
00:04:15.717 --> 00:04:18.760
"Did your mother and stepfather get a good price for the business?"

81
00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:19.540
I asked.

82
00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:23.804
"They didn't get nearly as much as my father would have if he were alive," she replied.

83
00:04:24.712 --> 00:04:29.235
I expected Holmes to be impatient with these minor details, but he listened with the greatest concentration.

84
00:04:29.255 --> 00:04:34.237
"Your own little income of one hundred pounds a year," said Holmes, "did that come out of the

85
00:04:34.277 --> 00:04:34.958
plumbing business?"

86
00:04:34.978 --> 00:04:36.558
"Oh no, sir.

87
00:04:37.359 --> 00:04:39.400
It was left to me by my uncle who died in New Zealand."

88
00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:44.363
"I believe that a single woman can live quite nicely on sixty pounds a year," said Holmes.

89
00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:49.485
"Yet, between your inheritance and your typing income, you have more than that."

90
00:04:50.426 --> 00:04:54.068
Miss Sutherland explained that she could easily live on less than sixty pounds a year.

91
00:04:54.956 --> 00:04:58.838
But she handed over to her stepfather the full one hundred pounds, plus her typing income.

92
00:04:58.858 --> 00:05:00.799
"You must understand, Mr.

93
00:05:00.839 --> 00:05:04.201
Holmes, that as long as I live at home, I don't want to be a burden to my

94
00:05:04.241 --> 00:05:05.422
parents," she said.

95
00:05:05.442 --> 00:05:08.864
"Of course, they only have that money while I continue to live with them."

96
00:05:09.724 --> 00:05:11.846
"You have made your position clear," said Holmes.

97
00:05:11.866 --> 00:05:14.447
"Now tell us all about your connection to Mr.

98
00:05:14.487 --> 00:05:15.207
Hosmer Angel."

99
00:05:16.088 --> 00:05:20.210
A flush stole over Miss Sutherland's face, and she picked nervously at the fringe on her jacket.

100
00:05:21.071 --> 00:05:23.092
"I met him at the Plumbers' Ball," she said.

101
00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:25.990
"Mr. Windibank did not want Mother and me to go.

102
00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:28.091
He never likes me to go anywhere.

103
00:05:28.111 --> 00:05:34.195
"In fact, he gets quite angry if I even suggest anything as innocent as a Sunday school picnic.

104
00:05:35.096 --> 00:05:36.277
But I was determined to go.

105
00:05:37.137 --> 00:05:39.459
What right did he have to keep me from enjoying myself?"

106
00:05:39.479 --> 00:05:42.701
"I can't understand his objections at all," I said.

107
00:05:42.721 --> 00:05:46.964
"He said that the people at the ball would be beneath us socially," said Miss Sutherland.

108
00:05:46.984 --> 00:05:50.086
"And he tried to argue that I had nothing suitable to wear.

109
00:05:50.847 --> 00:05:52.708
But I had a new dress that I'd never even worn."

110
00:05:53.524 --> 00:05:57.869
Mr. Windibank finally stopped arguing with her only because his employer sent him to France on business.

111
00:05:57.889 --> 00:06:02.655
"So Mother and I went to the ball in the company of our former foreman," said Miss Sutherland.

112
00:06:02.675 --> 00:06:05.819
"And it was there that I met the gentleman called Mr.

113
00:06:05.859 --> 00:06:06.640
Hosmer Angel."
